# Supabase Rules

All user-owned data must be protected with Row Level Security. Never trust a client-provided `user_id`. Use `auth.uid()` in RLS policies.

Progress photos must use a private storage bucket. Never expose the Supabase service-role key to the mobile application. Do not bypass RLS from client code.

Store storage paths, not permanent signed URLs. Generate signed URLs when private images need to be displayed.

Any child table belonging to a user's workout must verify ownership through its parent relationship.

Client env only: `EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL` and `EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`. The service-role key must never ship in the app.

# Database Rules

Migrations are the source of truth. Do not manually modify production schema without a migration. Every schema change must have a migration.

Use foreign keys. Use `ON DELETE CASCADE` where appropriate for user-owned child data. Add indexes for common user-scoped queries.

Use timestamps consistently. Prefer `timestamptz`. Do not store derived values unless there is a clear performance requirement.
